---@class azure.redhatopenshift.PlatformProfile
---@field managedResourceGroup? string The name of the resource group to put cluster resources in. If not specified then a unique name is generated from the following pattern "aro-hcp-" + clusterName + "-" + UUID where clusterName means the hcpOpenShiftClusters resource name (up to 45 characters) followed by a 16-byte universally unique identifier per RFC 4122.
---@field subnetId string The Azure resource ID of the worker subnet. Note that a subnet cannot be reused between ARO-HCP Clusters.
---@field vnetIntegrationSubnetId string The Azure resource ID of a subnet that enables direct, private network connectivity between the hosted control plane and your cluster's nodes. This subnet must be dedicated to ARO HCP and cannot be shared with the cluster subnet or any node pool subnets.
---@field outboundType? azure.redhatopenshift.PlatformProfileOutboundType The core outgoing configuration
---@field networkSecurityGroupId string ResourceId for the NSG (network security group) attached to the cluster subnet Note that NSGs cannot be reused for other ARO-HCP clusters.
